---
import SiteLayout from "../components/SiteLayout.astro";

const appUrl = "/help/getting-started/download-and-install/";
---

<SiteLayout title="Lapis Notes — a local-first desktop workspace">
  <main class="landing-main">
    <section class="landing-section landing-hero">
      <div class="landing-hero__copy">
        <p class="landing-kicker">Local files. Markdown. Extensible views.</p>
        <h1>Sharpen your notes.</h1>
        <p class="landing-hero__dek">
          Lapis Notes brings Markdown files, linked notes, and extensible views
          together in a local-first workspace. The Tauri Desktop app is
          currently a preview.
        </p>
        <div class="landing-actions">
          <a class="site-button site-button--primary" href={appUrl}
            >Explore Desktop</a
          >
          <a
            class="site-button site-button--secondary"
            href="/help/getting-started/create-a-vault/"
          >
            Read help
          </a>
          <a class="site-button site-button--secondary" href="/developers/"
            >Build plugins</a
          >
        </div>
        <ul class="landing-proof-list">
          <li>Ordinary Markdown files and folders</li>
          <li>
            Search, graph, and rich editing, with independently installed
            plugins
          </li>
          <li>A native Desktop preview for filesystem vaults</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <figure class="landing-shot" aria-label="Lapis Notes workspace preview">
        <div class="landing-window">
          <span></span>
          <span></span>
          <span></span>
          <strong>Notes</strong>
        </div>
        <img
          class="landing-shot__image"
          src="/media/desktop-workspace.light.webp"
          data-product-theme="light"
          alt="Lapis Notes workspace with the file explorer beside a rendered note."
          loading="eager"
        /><img
          class="landing-shot__image"
          src="/media/desktop-workspace.dark.webp"
          data-product-theme="dark"
          alt="Lapis Notes workspace with the file explorer beside a rendered note."
          loading="eager"
        />
      </figure>
    </section>

    <section class="landing-section landing-band">
      <div class="landing-band__copy">
        <p class="landing-eyebrow">Editing that stays portable</p>
        <h2>Use the markdown features you already rely on.</h2>
        <p>
          Lapis keeps the note itself primary, then layers live preview, embeds,
          properties, callouts, math, Mermaid, checklists, and code blocks over
          the same file.
        </p>
        <ul class="landing-feature-list">
          <li>Wikilinks, embeds, tags, and frontmatter-backed properties</li>
          <li>Tables, task lists, callouts, math blocks, and diagram fences</li>
          <li>Readable source plus richer rendered views when they help</li>
        </ul>
        <div class="landing-inline-actions">
          <a
            class="site-button site-button--secondary"
            href="/help/editing/markdown-basics/"
          >
            Explore editing docs
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
      <figure
        class="landing-shot landing-shot--feature"
        aria-label="Markdown editing preview"
      >
        <div class="landing-window">
          <span></span>
          <span></span>
          <span></span>
          <strong>Notes</strong>
        </div>
        <img
          class="landing-shot__image"
          src="/media/markdown-overview.light.webp"
          data-product-theme="light"
          alt="A rendered note with tables, callouts, and checklist items inside the Lapis Notes workspace."
          loading="lazy"
        /><img
          class="landing-shot__image"
          src="/media/markdown-overview.dark.webp"
          data-product-theme="dark"
          alt="A rendered note with tables, callouts, and checklist items inside the Lapis Notes workspace."
          loading="lazy"
        />
      </figure>
    </section>

    <section class="landing-section landing-band landing-band--reverse">
      <figure
        class="landing-shot landing-shot--feature"
        aria-label="Graph and canvas preview"
      >
        <div class="landing-window">
          <span></span>
          <span></span>
          <span></span>
          <strong>Graph &amp; canvas</strong>
        </div>
        <img
          class="landing-shot__image"
          src="/media/graph-banner.light.webp"
          data-product-theme="light"
          alt="Graph view showing relationships between notes in a Lapis workspace."
          loading="lazy"
        /><img
          class="landing-shot__image"
          src="/media/graph-banner.dark.webp"
          data-product-theme="dark"
          alt="Graph view showing relationships between notes in a Lapis workspace."
          loading="lazy"
        />
      </figure>
      <div class="landing-band__copy">
        <p class="landing-eyebrow">Move between views</p>
        <h2>Switch from linear notes to spatial and structured tools.</h2>
        <p>
          Follow links in graph view, arrange material on canvas boards, and
          turn note metadata into bases without moving work into a separate
          database.
        </p>
        <div class="landing-stack-grid">
          <article class="landing-stack-card">
            <h3>Graph and canvas</h3>
            <p>
              Explore relationships across the vault, then pin notes, files, and
              ideas into a board when layout matters more than document order.
            </p>
          </article>
          <article class="landing-stack-card">
            <h3>Bases and tasks</h3>
            <p>
              Build tables and cards from note properties with Bases. Tasks
              provides indexing and query tools; dedicated Tasks workspace views
              are still planned.
            </p>
          </article>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section
      class="landing-section landing-widget-section"
      aria-labelledby="landing-views-title"
    >
      <div class="landing-widget-section__copy">
        <p class="landing-eyebrow">Rich views, same files</p>
        <h2 id="landing-views-title">
          Preview notes, follow links, and lay out a board in the app.
        </h2>
        <p>
          Markdown previews, graph relationships, and canvas boards all read
          from the same vault files you edit elsewhere in the workspace.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="landing-showcase-rows">
        <article class="landing-band">
          <div class="landing-band__copy">
            <h3>Readable Markdown previews</h3>
            <p>
              Tables, callouts, math, checklists, and code blocks render from
              the same note content you keep in your vault.
            </p>
          </div>
          <figure
            class="landing-shot landing-shot--feature"
            aria-label="Markdown preview"
          >
            <div class="landing-window">
              <span></span>
              <span></span>
              <span></span>
              <strong>Notes</strong>
            </div>
            <img
              class="landing-shot__image"
              src="/media/markdown-overview.light.webp"
              data-product-theme="light"
              alt="A rendered note with tables, callouts, and checklist items inside the Lapis Notes workspace."
              loading="lazy"
            /><img
              class="landing-shot__image"
              src="/media/markdown-overview.dark.webp"
              data-product-theme="dark"
              alt="A rendered note with tables, callouts, and checklist items inside the Lapis Notes workspace."
              loading="lazy"
            />
          </figure>
        </article>

        <article class="landing-band landing-band--reverse">
          <div class="landing-band__copy">
            <h3>See how notes connect</h3>
            <p>
              Follow internal links, embeds, tags, and unresolved references
              across the vault in one relationship map.
            </p>
          </div>
          <figure
            class="landing-shot landing-shot--feature"
            aria-label="Graph view"
          >
            <div class="landing-window">
              <span></span>
              <span></span>
              <span></span>
              <strong>Graph</strong>
            </div>
            <img
              class="landing-shot__image"
              src="/media/graph-overview.light.webp"
              data-product-theme="light"
              alt="Graph view showing linked notes, tags, and unresolved references across a vault."
              loading="lazy"
            /><img
              class="landing-shot__image"
              src="/media/graph-overview.dark.webp"
              data-product-theme="dark"
              alt="Graph view showing linked notes, tags, and unresolved references across a vault."
              loading="lazy"
            />
          </figure>
        </article>

        <article class="landing-band">
          <div class="landing-band__copy">
            <h3>Arrange work on a board</h3>
            <p>
              Pin notes, tasks, and links on a canvas when spatial layout helps
              you plan or review a project.
            </p>
          </div>
          <figure
            class="landing-shot landing-shot--feature"
            aria-label="Canvas board"
          >
            <div class="landing-window">
              <span></span>
              <span></span>
              <span></span>
              <strong>Canvas</strong>
            </div>
            <img
              class="landing-shot__image"
              src="/media/canvas-banner.light.webp"
              data-product-theme="light"
              alt="A canvas board with linked notes, text cards, and connectors in the Lapis Notes workspace."
              loading="lazy"
            /><img
              class="landing-shot__image"
              src="/media/canvas-banner.dark.webp"
              data-product-theme="dark"
              alt="A canvas board with linked notes, text cards, and connectors in the Lapis Notes workspace."
              loading="lazy"
            />
          </figure>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section
      class="landing-section landing-evidence"
      aria-label="Workspace evidence"
    >
      <div class="landing-showcase-rows">
        <article class="landing-band">
          <div class="landing-band__copy">
            <p class="landing-eyebrow">Structured note views</p>
            <h3>Bases keep metadata useful without giving up files.</h3>
            <p>
              Turn frontmatter and task-note metadata into table and card views
              while keeping everything backed by ordinary vault content.
            </p>
          </div>
          <figure
            class="landing-shot landing-shot--feature"
            aria-label="Bases table view"
          >
            <div class="landing-window">
              <span></span>
              <span></span>
              <span></span>
              <strong>Bases</strong>
            </div>
            <img
              class="landing-shot__image"
              src="/media/bases-banner.light.webp"
              data-product-theme="light"
              alt="A Bases table view built from Markdown note properties inside a Lapis Notes workspace."
              loading="lazy"
            /><img
              class="landing-shot__image"
              src="/media/bases-banner.dark.webp"
              data-product-theme="dark"
              alt="A Bases table view built from Markdown note properties inside a Lapis Notes workspace."
              loading="lazy"
            />
          </figure>
        </article>

        <article class="landing-band landing-band--reverse">
          <div class="landing-band__copy">
            <p class="landing-eyebrow">Plugin surface</p>
            <h3>Plugins widen the workspace.</h3>
            <p>
              Desktop includes a core editing and navigation profile. Canvas,
              Bases, Notebook, Slides, and PDF are separately owned plugins;
              installation and host support vary. Check the plugin guides before
              enabling optional features.
            </p>
          </div>
          <figure
            class="landing-shot landing-shot--feature"
            aria-label="Community plugin settings"
          >
            <div class="landing-window">
              <span></span>
              <span></span>
              <span></span>
              <strong>Settings</strong>
            </div>
            <img
              class="landing-shot__image"
              src="/media/community-banner.light.webp"
              data-product-theme="light"
              alt="Community plugin settings in a Lapis workspace."
              loading="lazy"
            /><img
              class="landing-shot__image"
              src="/media/community-banner.dark.webp"
              data-product-theme="dark"
              alt="Community plugin settings in a Lapis workspace."
              loading="lazy"
            />
          </figure>
        </article>

        <article class="landing-band">
          <div class="landing-band__copy">
            <p class="landing-eyebrow">Notebook workflows</p>
            <h3>Keep executable analysis beside the note.</h3>
            <p>
              Mix prose, SQL, JavaScript cells, and interactive inputs in
              `.notebook.md` files so analysis stays beside the notes it
              supports.
            </p>
          </div>
          <figure
            class="landing-shot landing-shot--feature"
            aria-label="Notebook gallery"
          >
            <div class="landing-window">
              <span></span>
              <span></span>
              <span></span>
              <strong>Notebook</strong>
            </div>
            <img
              class="landing-shot__image"
              src="/media/notebook-workspace.light.webp"
              data-product-theme="light"
              alt="A notebook with executed cells inside a Lapis Notes workspace."
              loading="lazy"
            /><img
              class="landing-shot__image"
              src="/media/notebook-workspace.dark.webp"
              data-product-theme="dark"
              alt="A notebook with executed cells inside a Lapis Notes workspace."
              loading="lazy"
            />
          </figure>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="landing-section landing-platforms">
      <div>
        <p class="landing-eyebrow">Runs where your vault lives</p>
        <h2>Start with the Desktop preview.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="landing-platforms__body">
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>Web app</strong> uses browser-managed storage for a browser vault;
            capabilities and availability differ from Desktop.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Desktop</strong> opens filesystem folders as vaults through the
            native Tauri shell. Preview archives are available for macOS Apple Silicon
            and Linux ARM64/x64; review the release's platform limitations.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Local-first</strong> means your notes remain ordinary vault files
            that can be backed up, synced, or inspected with other tools.
          </li>
        </ul>
        <div class="landing-closing-card">
          <h3>Start with a vault, then grow into views and plugins.</h3>
          <p>
            The help docs cover vault setup, editing, plugins, and the desktop
            and web workflows needed to make the app feel at home.
          </p>
          <div class="landing-inline-actions">
            <a class="site-button site-button--primary" href="/help/"
              >Browse help</a
            >
            <a class="site-button site-button--secondary" href="/developers/"
              >Read developer docs</a
            >
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</SiteLayout>
